 Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","review_id":"usP8ij__LdUlzVLdBcWp7g","date":"2015-09-16T15:52:47","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9514151215553284,"text_excerpt":"** Hot Spot Alert ** This place was suggested by one of my very good NOLA Yelp friends. So glad I managed to eat here. The U shaped bar is the place where you can have the max experience of this place because they have a really awesome day time bartender (jeez - forgot her name, but she is the life of the bar area, works hard and thoroughly enjoys working there - her words, \"I love working here because anyone who comes here, goes happy. What more can you ask for?\" #TrueThat!) Testament to that - the very awesome Bloody Mary that she fixed. Spicy, with some magic potion in it; wish I had the secret recipe, but then again, a very solid excuse to visit NOLA soon. Those pickled string beans? ..."},{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","review_id":"3BlhQRuC1fiWxPYpwUcl0Q","date":"2016-01-02T15:09:22","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9484286904335022,"text_excerpt":"I love this place. It's close quarters but not too noisy. The staff is very friendly and a few of them are funny. They make you feel very welcomed. I tried the seafood gumbo - good stuff; not hot sauce spike needed because it packs just the right kick. And it's packed with meat. So the jambalaya has sausage and rabbit in it. Wasn't sure how I was gonna feel about it at first. The verdict: yummy. You must try it. And the fried chicken - you need to mane sure you get at least one piece of chicken before you leave. These people know what they are doing!"},{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","review_id":"-8mFomW4a9vYPJ3xzh0WHA","date":"2010-11-02T16:56:01","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9483119249343872,"text_excerpt":"Visited New Orleans and stopped by Coops. There was a line, but there were bar seats available. Had the tasting plate and an Abita beer (local). The gumbo was good, the fried chicken was tender and tasty, the rabbit and sausage jambalaya was amazing. Overall great food. The place is a little small and looks more like a rundown bar, but I'm not complaining. The service can also be a little friendlier. But the jambalaya trumps all."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","photo_id":"TcrJX4z8esDqoACVo02VJQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/TcrJX4z8esDqoACVo02VJQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8599264621734619},{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","photo_id":"aHvZVvENLY30_Ef_7aDB4g","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/aHvZVvENLY30_Ef_7aDB4g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8429583311080933},{"business_id":"XnQ84ylyAZwh-XfHGGNBbQ","photo_id":"6IN3K0OtrHNXaNx9GhdTFg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/6IN3K0OtrHNXaNx9GhdTFg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8397350311279297},{"business_id":"XnQ